Using "final" Keyword in JAVA:
* final keyword is non-access modifier used to restrict from 
  further modifying variables,methods and class 
* if final is used for variable declaration means that value will no modify 
  Ex:
      final int val=1216;
* if final is used for method means not possible to override in sub class
  Ex:
     final void display(){
	  ------
	 }
* if final is used for class means not possible to inherit
  Ex:
     final class Vehicle{
	  ------
	 }